instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-follow — the line in plays the patch: its pitch, its loudness and its attacks move
; everything, the hands only steer. A second singer, an envelope-driven echo chamber, an attack
; sequencer for a cave, and a spectral gate that listens. Line/Mic switch to line.
;
; every scene:
;   fader1 (Mix)     how much of the processing against the line
;   fader2 (Decay)   how hard the line pushes the processing (depth of the follower)
;   fader3 (Volume)  the scene's colour (formant, tone, room)
;   keys1            an interval or a root (C none, up to B); octave1 an octave down or up
;   keys2            a second root, or a scale step
;   mode1            held: the follower lets go (what it last heard stays)
;   left LED         what the ear hears (loudness or pitch);  right LED  what it plays
; Step through the scenes with a held Mode button and a tap on the other.

a second singer
---------------
; a second voice, the line's own, sung an interval above it (the bottom key: C unison, G a
; fifth...), formants kept so a voice stays a voice; fader3 moves the formants on purpose,
; fader1 from the line alone to the second voice alone.
the second is psola samplerate=half
line.both -> second
the oct1 is transpose
the mix is crossfade
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9 samplerate=half
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.key -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> second.pitch
fader3 -> second.formant
line.both -> mix.a
second -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
mix -> guard
guard -> out
line.both -> lights.left
second -> lights.right

the chamber breathes
--------------------
; the louder the line, the brighter a band filter opens on it and the shorter the echo gets; the
; quieter, the longer the tail. Hold mode1 and every attack repeats its last slice (a beat
; repeat that shrinks); the top keys make the slice longer (C short, B long). fader2 how far the
; loudness pushes, fader3 how much of the room; fader1 the echo against the line.
the ear is follower attack=0.005 release=0.3
the hits is onset sensitivity=0.5
the bright is svf 6 res=0.4
the push is vca
the calm is attenuverter amount=-1 offset=0.7
the repeat is stutter decay=0.6 shrink=0.3
the only is vca
the echo is pingpong 3 time=0.5
the room is reverblite 3 size=0.6
the roomlevel is vca
the mix is crossfade

line.both -> ear hits bright
ear -> push
fader2 -> push.gain
push -> bright.cutoff
push -> calm
calm -> echo.feedback
bright.band -> repeat
hits.pulse -> only
mode1 -> only.gain
only -> repeat.trig
keys2.key -20> repeat.length
repeat -> echo
echo.l echo.r -> room
room -> roomlevel
fader3 -> roomlevel.gain
line.both -> mix.a
echo.l -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
mix roomlevel -> left
mix echo.r roomlevel -> right
ear -> lights.left
hits.pulse -> lights.right

the attack sequencer
--------------------
; every attack in the line takes a step through eight notes and strikes a cave tuned to that
; step (the Wingie's threshold sequencer, grown up). The bottom keys transpose the sequence;
; a top key held stops it on its step. The cave's ring goes through grains that sing it back
; at the top key's step above; fader2 how long the cave rings, fader3 how dense the grains.
the hits is onset sensitivity=0.5
the steps is seq 8: 0 3 7 10 12 10 7 5
the stop is vca
the go is attenuverter amount=-1 offset=1
the root is transpose
the cave is cave 2 samplerate=half
the sing is grains 2 samplerate=half window=gauss spread=0.7
the up is transpose
the mix is crossfade
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> hits cave
hits.pulse -> stop
keys2.gate -> go
go -> stop.gain                   ; a held top key: no steps
stop -> steps.next cave.strike
octave1 -> root
keys1.key -> root.pitch
steps root -> cave.shift
fader2 -> cave.decay
cave -> sing
octave2 -> up
keys2.key -> up.pitch
up -> sing.pitch
fader3 -> sing.density
mode1 -> sing.freeze
line.both -> mix.a
cave -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
mix sing.left -> guardl
mix sing.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
hits.env -> lights.left
steps.pulse -> lights.right

the gate that listens
---------------------
; a spectral gate lets only the loud partials of the line through (fader2 how loud they must be);
; play softly and it closes further, loud and it opens. What passes is played backwards in
; slices (fader1 from forwards to all reversed) whose size follows how sure the ear is of a pitch:
; a sung note gives long slices, noise short ones. Hold mode1 and the gate keeps only the hiss.
; fader3 how wide the stereo.
the sieve is specgate 1 samplerate=quarter
the hiss is specgate 1 samplerate=quarter keep=quiet
the which is crossfade
the ear is follower attack=0.01 release=0.4 samplerate=half
the sure is pitchtrack samplerate=quarter
the back is reverse samplerate=half
the wide is widener samplerate=quarter
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9 samplerate=half

line.both -> sieve hiss ear sure
fader2 -> sieve.threshold hiss.threshold
ear -30> sieve.threshold
sieve -> which.a
hiss -> which.b
mode1 -> which.mix
which -> back
fader1 -> back.mix
sure.confidence -> back.size
back -> guard -> wide
fader3 -> wide.width
wide.left -> left
wide.right -> right
ear -> lights.left
sure.confidence -> lights.right
